FILE: app/src/jump-to-frame.ts
```ts
import { goToFrame, playAnimation } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import type { AnimationGroup } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function jumpToFrame(group: AnimationGroup, frame: number): void {
    goToFrame(group, frame);
    playAnimation(group);
}
```

I created `src/jump-to-frame.ts` with a two-step implementation: `goToFrame` seeks the group to the given frame (it converts the frame to seconds via the group's `frameRate`, wraps on looping groups, clamps on non-looping ones, writes the pose, and pauses), then `playAnimation` resumes from that point, preserving the group's `speedRatio` and `loopAnimation`. Nothing I was unsure of — the notes make the behavior of both functions explicit enough to be confident.
